# Copy this file to ".env" and fill in your webhook URL.
# Never commit .env — it is git-ignored.
#
# ===== DISCORD (recommended for demo — free) =====
#
# 1. Open Discord → your team server (or create one).
# 2. Create a channel e.g. #coast-alerts (or use any channel).
# 3. Channel settings (gear icon) → Integrations → Webhooks → New Webhook.
# 4. Name it "C.O.A.S.T. Alert" → Copy Webhook URL → paste below.
# 5. Save. Anyone in that channel will see alert messages during the demo.
#
# Quick test (PowerShell, paste your URL):
#   Invoke-RestMethod -Uri "YOUR_WEBHOOK_URL" -Method Post -ContentType "application/json" -Body '{"content":"C.O.A.S.T. test OK"}'
#
DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL=https://discord.com/api/webhooks/1531425443574579251/C--jWwk3_Pa4md-vdTWkKfHjDxBdWkPMoHSm1UXlr0nVRe24cv2WAlTMKNtQmPOt8e1o
#
# ===== TELEGRAM (optional) =====
# Leave blank unless you use Telegram instead of Discord.
#
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=
